  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions about roofing in Richardson</h2>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Who is the best roofing contractor in Richardson, TX?</h3><p>Our top pick for 2026 is Richardson Roofing Pro, headquartered on W Arapaho Rd inside Richardson and serving the area since 1992. Helsley Roofing Company, a Plano-based contractor with 30 years in business and membership in the North Texas Roofing Contractors Association, is a strong second option.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Will homeowners insurance cover a roof replacement in Richardson after hail?</h3><p>Often, yes. Richardson sits within North Texas's active hail corridor, and many roofs here are replaced through insurance claims following spring storms. Expect to pay your wind/hail deductible, typically 1-2% of your dwelling coverage on North Texas policies.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>How much does a new roof cost in Richardson, TX?</h3><p>Most full replacements run $9,500-$18,000 for architectural shingles, with the DFW-wide median around $12,500-$15,000. Class 4 impact-resistant shingles, which some insurers discount premiums for, run $12,000-$18,000.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>How do I avoid storm-chasing roofers in Richardson?</h3><p>Confirm a real, checkable business address, ask how long the company has operated in North Texas specifically (not just claims of general industry experience), and be wary of any contractor who arrives door-to-door immediately after a storm asking you to sign before your insurance adjuster has inspected the roof.</p></div>
